            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that Congress updated the child\u2011pornography statutes in 1996 to cover virtual images, asserting the provisions are constitutional because they are similar to earlier upheld laws."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e0609f71658fef7612e4b0d9df0c3fffed11f24367b810332df5e4bf9039df3e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e0609f71658f-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court asked whether any prior case had been lost on the ground of overbreadth."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e0609f71658fef7612e4b0d9df0c3fffed11f24367b810332df5e4bf9039df3e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e0609f71658f-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Court, justices questioned whether the statute would prohibit a motion\u2011picture company from employing an 18\u2011year\u2011old actress."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e0609f71658fef7612e4b0d9df0c3fffed11f24367b810332df5e4bf9039df3e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e0609f71658f-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice O'Connor asked whether the statute is overbroad, suggesting that overbreadth is the respondent's problem."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e0609f71658fef7612e4b0d9df0c3fffed11f24367b810332df5e4bf9039df3e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e0609f71658f-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, justices inquired whether the amendments to the statutes eliminated the requirement that material be patently offensive."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "e0609f71658fef7612e4b0d9df0c3fffed11f24367b810332df5e4bf9039df3e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-e0609f71658f-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice, another question concerned protecting real children when experts cannot distinguish virtual from real depictions."
      }
